message: "If you use or discuss this work, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "A Universal Scaling Law for Ellipse Perimeters"
type: article
authors:
  - family-names: Baker
    given-names: Wayne
date-released: 2026-07-14
version: revised-preprint-v1.2
repository-code: "https://github.com/CWBaker360/universal-scaling-law-ellipse-perimeters"
url: "https://github.com/CWBaker360/universal-scaling-law-ellipse-perimeters"
abstract: >-
  For equal-parameter polygonal approximations of a nondegenerate ellipse,
  the polygonal perimeter factors exactly into a universal sinc term and a
  periodic midpoint quadrature. Analytic periodic quadrature makes the latter
  exponentially accurate, yielding universal algebraic relative-error
  coefficients and a fourth-order tripling correction.
keywords:
  - ellipse perimeter
  - polygonal approximation
  - sinc scaling
  - Richardson extrapolation
  - N-series
  - periodic trapezoidal rule
  - asymptotic analysis
  - constructive geometry
license: proprietary
